  "interpretation": [
    "Checkpoint5 promotes less often than checkpoint2 on identical states, but forcing all its waits to promotion does not improve net wins against checkpoint2 in this sample.",
    "Eight checkpoint5 policy waits disagree with search promotion recommendations; one Chronomon root changes losses to wins against checkpoint2 and checkpoint4 under policy continuations.",
    "The selected SW root is a candidate search/value failure: search waits under five seeds, and a full-search actor continuation wins after promotion but loses after waiting against checkpoint2. One true hidden realization does not prove an engine bug or establish an expected-value failure across hidden worlds.",
    "No directional opponent-age effect was detected: the estimated change in wait advantage against checkpoint6 versus checkpoint2 is zero, with wide uncertainty.",
    "Investigate the saved SW search/value counterexample and target-to-policy disagreements before making promotion a rule or changing the opponent pool."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Exploratory fixed-pool screen; four roots per archetype do not establish per-deck strength.",
    "Search is exact-composition open-decklist PIMC, not a closed-decklist test.",
    "Policy continuation outcomes alone cannot prove a search/value defect: a searched choice may require searched follow-up play.",
    "No incomplete continuation counts as a draw; source games without a completed result are not sampled.",
    "One actual hidden-state realization per root; 4-world root search does not make the continuation four independent games.",
    "Search seed sensitivity and searched continuations target one SW counterexample selected after inspecting the screen; they are exploratory, not independent population estimates.",
    "These are counterfactual continuations from sampled midgame states, not full-game matchup win rates."
  ],
